# Maestro E2E Mobile Tests

Generate and maintain Maestro test flows for React Native and Flutter apps.

## Flow structure

```yaml
# .maestro/flows/<category>/<flow-name>.yaml
appId: com.example.app
---
- launchApp
- assertVisible: "Screen Title"
- tapOn:
    id: "testID"
- assertVisible: "Next Screen"
```

## File organization

```text
.maestro/
├── config.yaml          ← App ID, defaults
├── flows/
│   ├── auth/
│   │   ├── login-success.yaml
│   │   └── login-error.yaml
│   ├── onboarding/
│   │   └── complete-onboarding.yaml
│   └── <feature>/
│       └── <scenario>.yaml
└── utils/
    ├── login.yaml       ← Reusable sub-flows
    └── navigate-to.yaml
```

## Command reference

| Action | Maestro YAML |
|--------|-------------|
| Tap button | `tapOn: { id: "testID" }` or `tapOn: "Label"` |
| Type text | `inputText: { id: "testID", text: "value" }` |
| Assert visible | `assertVisible: "Text"` or `assertVisible: { id: "testID" }` |
| Assert NOT visible | `assertNotVisible: "Error"` |
| Scroll | `scroll` |
| Swipe | `swipe: { direction: "up" }` |
| Back button | `pressKey: "back"` |
| Long press | `longPressOn: "Element"` |
| Wait | `assertVisible: { text: "Ready", enabled: true }` |
| Sub-flow | `runFlow: utils/login.yaml` |

## Rules

1. One flow per user journey (5-15 steps max)
2. Prefer `testID` over text matching (stable selectors)
3. Assert screen arrival after every navigation
4. Reusable sequences go in `utils/` as sub-flows
5. Name flows descriptively: `login-success.yaml`, not `test1.yaml`
6. Include both happy path and primary error case
7. Add YAML comments for non-obvious waits or assertions

## From Figma

When generating from a Figma flow:
1. Identify each frame as a screen
2. Identify arrows/connections as navigation actions
3. Map button labels to `tapOn` commands
4. Map screen titles to `assertVisible` assertions
5. Generate one flow per connected sequence

## Missing testIDs

If implementation lacks testIDs, report what's needed:

```
⚠️ Missing testIDs:
- PaymentScreen submit button → suggest: testID="payment-submit"
- CartScreen amount input → suggest: testID="cart-amount-input"
```

Do NOT generate flows that rely on brittle text matching when testIDs should exist.

## Running

```bash
maestro test .maestro/flows/auth/login-success.yaml   # Single flow
maestro test .maestro/flows/                           # All flows
maestro test --dry-run .maestro/flows/                 # Validate YAML only
```
